SearchBox.tsx (no debounce yet):

useEffect(() => {
  if (!query) return;
  fetch(`https://api.codedev.test/courses?search=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`)
    .then((res) => res.json())
    .then(setResults);
}, [query]);

Network panel after typing "react" quickly (request, then time until the response finished):
?search=r      t=0 ms     110 ms
?search=re     t=60 ms    900 ms   <- finished last, at t=960
?search=rea    t=120 ms   130 ms
?search=reac   t=180 ms   120 ms
?search=react  t=240 ms   150 ms

The box shows "react", the list shows the results for "re".

Statement: "Returning a cleanup from this effect that aborts the request (an AbortController per run, controller.abort() in the cleanup) would keep the \"re\" response from replacing the \"react\" results."

A Vitest test for the debounced search hook (debounce 300 ms):

vi.useFakeTimers();
const search = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue([]);
const box = createDebouncedSearch({ debounceMs: 300, search, ... });
box.onInput("react");
vi.advanceTimersByTime(299);
expect(search).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(0);   // passes
vi.advanceTimersByTime(1);
expect(search).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);   // passes

 Test Files  1 passed (1)
 Duration  41ms

Statement: "Because the whole test runs in 41 ms, it cannot prove the 300 ms delay; only a test that really waits 300 ms can check the debounce."
